        "id": 1003224
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-12T20:07:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "while i think there\u0027s an argument that that would be fine _for bionic_, it\u0027s not true for ndk api in general, and is the whole reason they want the llndk to lag behind?",
      "parentUuid": "f8429635_a4321157",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 326,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 326,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "7ddf11eccf4e5faa2ce6b2b277a6fb7232f7252d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e764002_1de860da",
        "filename": "cc/symbolfile/__init__.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 326,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-12T20:58:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It should be fine for all NDK libraries (which are also LL-NDK libraries, the only ones this matters for). LL-NDK has always implicitly included NDK APIs, using \u002736\u0027 would mean that we have the same behavior here that we\u0027ve always had for the LL-NDK/NDK in Android.\n\nLeaving it 35 means that the trend set by Trunk Stable, which allows for LL-NDK and NDK APIs to be defined at separate times, to continue moving forward. The reason the LL-NDK had to lag behind for 202404/34 was because the LL-NDK API was frozen 1 quarter earlier last year.\n\nLeaving it as 35 is also the most flexible choice possible here, which is why I put it in the CL itself. It\u0027s my preference beacuse:\n- pro: makes Android V start a trend, rather than being special\n- pro: allows us to specify LL-NDK/NDK membership independently this year\n- con: requires two lines of .txt for an API to be included in 202404 and 36",
      "parentUuid": "349a258f_95b7894f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 326,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 326,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "7ddf11eccf4e5faa2ce6b2b277a6fb7232f7252d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "598e478e_7c118a27",
        "filename": "cc/symbolfile/__init__.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 326,
      "author": {
        "id": 1043845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-12T21:20:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Leaving it 35 means that the trend set by Trunk Stable, which allows for LL-NDK and NDK APIs to be defined at separate times\n\nThat\u0027s not one of the things trunk stable does afaik. Even if that\u0027s the plan, nothing about trunk stable applies to native APIs because the work needed to support it was never funded.\n\nI think the LL-NDK is approaching this as-if the _implementation_ could be separately stabilized. The map files define what\u0027s in the stubs and when something is added to each set of stubs can vary, but I can\u0027t think of a good reason to do so (aside from promoting LL-NDK APIs to the NDK, which is uncommon, and I\u0027ve never seen the reverse happen). There\u0027s only one implementation though. Trunk stable (that is, feature flags) can\u0027t change that. The LL-NDK has to finalize the implementation on the same schedule as the rest of the platform.\n\n\u003e pro: makes Android V start a trend, rather than being special\n\nA trend of what? I don\u0027t follow.\n\n\u003e pro: allows us to specify LL-NDK/NDK membership independently this year\n\nBeing _able_ to do that is one thing. Being _required_ to do that for every API is a con. The LL-NDK should inherit from the NDK by default and opt-out in the rare cases where that\u0027s necessary.",
      "parentUuid": "3e764002_1de860da",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 326,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 326,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "7ddf11eccf4e5faa2ce6b2b277a6fb7232f7252d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f2f61b9f_27aca670",
        "filename": "cc/symbolfile/__init__.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 326,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-12T23:00:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think the LL-NDK is approaching this as-if the implementation could be separately stabilized.\n\nTrunk Stable did apply to LL-NDK in Android V and that work was done and approved. If you want to make changes to that, I can put you in touch with the right people. Let me know! We can\u0027t exactly rewrite the past.\n\n\u003e The LL-NDK has to finalize the implementation on the same schedule as the rest of the platform.\n\nThis change gives you the choice for Android W, you can have it either way, up to you. If you want to make statements about what can ever happen in the future, you\u0027ll need to pursue that separately as it\u0027s way above what I can say. I can say flexibility in the code is great though!",
      "parentUuid": "598e478e_7c118a27",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 326,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 326,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "7ddf11eccf4e5faa2ce6b2b277a6fb7232f7252d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2de7d811_065d9222",
        "filename": "cc/symbolfile/__init__.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 326,
      "author": {
        "id": 1043845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-12T23:07:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e\u003e I think the LL-NDK is approaching this as-if the implementation could be separately stabilized.\n\u003e\n\u003e Trunk Stable did apply to LL-NDK in Android V and that work was done and approved\n\n\"trunk stable\" as in \"it\u0027s all \u0027one\u0027 branch now\" did. Flagging did not. The plumbing simply does not exist.\n\n\u003e\u003e The LL-NDK has to finalize the implementation on the same schedule as the rest of the platform.\n\u003e\n\u003e This change gives you the choice for Android W\n\nHow? There\u0027s only one implementation. It\u0027s finalized or it isn\u0027t. What am I missing?",
      "parentUuid": "f2f61b9f_27aca670",
